---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LightsOutStudy from '../components/LightsOutStudy.astro';
---
<Layout isHome={true}>
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
 <div class="hero-art"></div><div class="hero-shade"></div>
 <div class="shell hero-inner"><p class="kicker"><span></span> Audience strategy for independent film</p>
 <h1 id="hero-title">Who will show up<br/>for <em>your film?</em></h1>
 <p class="intro">For independent producers and distributors planning a US release. We review your cut to find your first audience, the scene that sells the ticket, and the edits worth testing.</p>
 <div class="actions"><a class="button hot" href="#contact">Discuss your film</a><a class="text-link" href="#case-study">See the <em>Lights Out</em> study</a></div>
 </div>
</section>
<section class="service" id="service"><div class="shell">
 <p class="kicker ink"><span></span> The service</p><div class="service-head"><h2>From the cut to<br/><em>the campaign.</em></h2><p>Before you lock the trailer, buy media, or take a feature to buyers, choose the decision you need to make. We watch the full film and compare it against eleven audience profiles.</p></div>
 <div class="deliverables">
 <article><div class="icon audience-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><h3>Find your first audience</h3><p>See who has the strongest reason to watch, which scenes earn their interest, and who you could lose by broadening the pitch.</p></article>
 <article><div class="icon frame-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></div><h3>Choose the trailer opening</h3><p>Get two written openings or buyer pitches tied to timecodes, with a plan to test which one moves people closer to buying a ticket.</p></article>
 <article><div class="icon edits-icon" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><h3>Know what to change</h3><p>See where a trim, a sound cue, or one more beat could help. Each edit names who might gain interest and who might miss what you cut.</p></article>
 </div>
 <details><summary>How does the audience analysis work?</summary><p>We use AI-assisted video and audio analysis to score scenes for what different viewers enjoy, from immediate danger to emotional payoff. An analyst checks decisive moments against your cut. We then use US audience research to suggest age groups, theater catchments, and Facebook, Instagram and TikTok tests. Actual ticket sales tell you whether to expand.</p></details>
 </div></section>
<LightsOutStudy />
<section class="contact" id="contact"><div class="shell contact-grid"><div><p class="kicker ink"><span></span> Work with us</p><h2>Bring us your<br/><em>release decision.</em></h2><p class="offer"><strong>$1,500</strong> per feature engagement</p><p class="offer-copy">One authorized feature, one decision, and a written brief in five business days from agreed scope and receipt of the cut. Includes a 30-minute working session and one review of your test results.</p><p class="fine">We can agree an NDA, screener access and processing terms before you share your film.</p></div>
 <form action="/inquiries" method="post" id="inquiry"><h3>Tell us about your film</h3><div class="pair"><label>Your name<input required name="name" autocomplete="name" maxlength="100"/></label><label>Work email<input required type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" maxlength="254"/></label></div>
 <label>Film or working title<input name="film" required maxlength="180"/></label><label>What decision are you facing?<textarea name="decision" rows="3" maxlength="2500" required placeholder="For example, choosing a trailer opening before a festival sale."></textarea></label>
 <div class="trap" aria-hidden="true"><label>Leave this blank<input name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"/></label></div>
 <button class="button dark" type="submit">Send inquiry</button><p class="form-note">Send a short note. We’ll reply by email. Please keep screener links and confidential material for later.</p>
 <p class="feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
 <a class="email" href="mailto:hello@synthworx.com">hello@synthworx.com</a>
 </form></div></section>
</Layout>
<script>
 const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#inquiry')!;
 form.addEventListener('submit', async e=>{
   e.preventDefault();
   const button=form.querySelector('button')!,feedback=form.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.feedback')!;
   button.disabled=true;feedback.textContent='Sending…';
   try {
    const response=await fetch(form.action,{method:'POST',headers:{Accept:'application/json'},body:new URLSearchParams(new FormData(form) as unknown as Record<string,string>)});
    const result=await response.json();if(!response.ok)throw new Error(result.message || 'Please try again or email us directly.');
    form.reset();feedback.textContent='Thank you. Your inquiry is in our inbox.';
   } catch(err){feedback.textContent=err instanceof Error && !(err instanceof TypeError)?err.message:'We couldn’t confirm delivery. Please try again or email us directly.'}
   finally{button.disabled=false}
 });
</script>
